        "like": 2
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I understand VRC is never private, but I would never ever feel comfortable having software that's actively waiting for me to say a phrase its looking for to then send and record to other services and then back to vrchat staff.  I watched this overview video below, and it seems like it keeps a lot of data that could potentially aid in context, letting you go back in segments of minutes.  \nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yGt7B59NmDk\nModulate also appears to build profiles on users(albeit with \"anonymized\" identifiers) based on their voice. This is something that is extremely uncomfortable to me.\nIf vrc did implement something like this I'd have to deeply consider stopping my own use of the platform.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
