      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "629574688664e30b6bd76d93",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is in my opinion a bad idea,\n\nAfter the EAC update I've seen a huge decrease in toxicity in VRChat,\n\nbut putting this in the game feels like a big violation of the privacy from the user.\n\nI rarely see someone toxic walking around nowadays and it feels like toxicity was largely linked to (malicious) client users.\n\nWhat I would suggest when people start to play VRChat is to learn to self moderate their experience by for example letting them go through a tutorial or keeping them reminded trough the quick menu information section.\n\nI really thing the new groups feature and self-moderation and reminding people about the self-moderation tools is the way to go.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
